faciolock (0.1.0~ppa3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Daylight. The emitter check asked for a dark OFF frame, which ambient
    infrared never gives it; it now asks for modulation instead. Every frame
    pair must show OFF/ON <= 0.9 and ON-OFF >= 5 levels, and both are enforced
    rather than advisory. Recorded daylight captures enrol and verify with
    these defaults. A daylight run on hardware is still owed.
  * What that costs: the margin the darkness threshold held against a pulsed
    infrared source does not carry over, and extra infrared beside a genuinely
    enrolled face is not categorically rejected.
  * The detector's score floor rose from 0.3 to 0.8.
  * faciolockctl diagnose reports modulation and signal/noise in place of a
    bright/dark ratio, and its advice no longer blames the room.
  * README.Debian and faciolockctl(1) said daylight refuses. They no longer do.
  * A printed face is still not reliably rejected.
  * Enable the face PAM profile by default and add a system-wide On/Off toggle
    through faciolockctl and the Plasma settings page.
  * Start face scanning automatically at SDDM login and Plasma screen unlock;
    show a scanning indicator while checking and keep password fallback.
  * Limit each camera attempt to six seconds and release it after capture.

 -- Somesh Rao <cokasomeshrao@outlook.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:43:21 +0530

faciolock (0.1.0~ppa2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * A settings page, so enrolment stops requiring a terminal.
  * New binary package plasma-faciolock-kcm: a KDE System Settings module and
    a matching "Face Unlock" launcher entry. It holds no privilege of its own
    and runs faciolockctl through the existing polkit action. It will not turn
    face authentication on or off; that stays with pam-auth-update.
  * faciolockctl gained "status", which needs no root and touches no camera.
  * Fix: a closed stdin captured all three enrolment poses back to back,
    without waiting for the person to move, and saved them as a complete
    enrolment. It never failed, so it was never noticed.
  * The panel's QML modules are declared by hand. They are compiled into the
    plugin as a Qt resource, where dh_shlibdeps cannot find them, and without
    them the page loads blank.
  * GNOME and GDM remain untested rather than claimed.

 -- Somesh Rao <cokasomeshrao@outlook.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0530

faciolock (0.1.0~ppa1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release; the first packaged build.
  * Three binary packages: faciolock (daemon, CLI, units), libpam-faciolock
    (the module and its pam-auth-update profile), faciolock-models (weights).
  * Face authentication ships disabled. The profile registers at
    "Default: no", so pam-auth-update leaves every stack untouched until an
    administrator enables it.
  * Known limitations at this version, both measured rather than suspected:
    face authentication refuses in bright daylight, and a printed face is not
    reliably rejected by the liveness checks.

 -- Somesh Rao <cokasomeshrao@outlook.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:57:01 +0530
